  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "Prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates, a close boarded timber fence, 1.8m in height as measured from ground level adjacent to each panel, shall be erected along the boundaries of the external amenity spaces of the site. All fencing shall accord with BS 1722 5:2006 and shall be retained for a period of at least five years. \r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012. \r",
    "The flat roof areas of the development to which this permission relates shall not be used as a roof garden, balcony, seating area or other similar amenity area, and shall not be accessed except for the purpose of maintenance or in the case of emergency. \r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012. \r",
    "The cycle parking facilities as shown on the approved plans shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained for that purpose and kept free from obstruction thereafter. \r\rReason: To ensure that appropriate opportunities to promote sustainable transport are taken up, in accordance with policy T5 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS6 and DM8 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012. \r",
    "The refuse and recycling facilities as shown on the approved plans shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained thereafter. The developer and/or their successors in title shall take all reasonable steps to ensure that all refuse and recyclable materials associated with the development are either stored within these facilities or internally within the building(s) on the application site, and that no refuse or recycling material is stored or placed for collection on the public highway except on the day of collection. \r\rReason: To ensure proper waste management in the interests of the character and appearance of the area and the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy SI17 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012. \r",
    "The dwellings hereby approved shall be designed and constructed to achieve a maximum water consumption of no more than 105 litres per person per day (as calculated in accordance with the Building Regulations Optional Requirement G2), and shall thereafter be retained as such. \r\rReason: To ensure the development is sustainable and minimises water consumption in accordance with Policy SI5 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM3 of the LDF Core Strategy (2012).\r",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved Fire Safety Strategy (prepared by Redwoods, dated 29/10/2025) and thereafter maintained. \r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users, in accordance with Policy D12 of the London Plan 2021. \r"
  ],
